.TH SPRITESTUDIO-CLI 1 "September 2026" "SpriteStudio 0.11.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
spritestudio-cli \- headless 2D sprite atlas packer, slicer, filter and batch exporter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B spritestudio-cli
[\fIFLAVOR_OPTIONS\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIINPUT_FILES\fR...]
.br
.B spritestudio-cli
\fISUBCOMMAND\fR [\fISUBCOMMAND_OPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B TexturePacker
[\fITEXTUREPACKER_COMPATIBLE_OPTIONS\fR] [\fIINPUT_FILES\fR...]
.br
.B aseprite
\-b [\fIASEPRITE_COMPATIBLE_OPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B spritestudio-cli
is the non-interactive, headless command-line counterpart of the SpriteStudio 2D sprite preparation suite.
It executes without any graphic display server or X11/Wayland dependencies (\fBQT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen\fR),
making it suitable for studio continuous integration (CI/CD) pipelines, automated build scripts, and game engine asset compilation.
.PP
The tool features an automatic flavor dispatcher (\fBCliDispatcher\fR) allowing it to function either with native subcommands
or as a seamless 100% drop-in replacement for \fBTexturePacker\fR and \fBAseprite\fR batch invocations.

.SH FLAVORS AND MODES OF OPERATION
The operating mode is automatically inferred from the binary invocation name (\fBargv[0]\fR) or explicitly selected via \fB\-\-flavor\fR:
.TP
.B texturepacker
Activated when invoked as \fBTexturePacker\fR or with \fB\-\-flavor=texturepacker\fR. Accepts all standard TexturePacker flags and generates matching JSON, Godot, or XML formats.
.TP
.B aseprite
Activated when invoked as \fBaseprite\fR with \fB\-b\fR (\-\-batch) or with \fB\-\-flavor=aseprite\fR. Accepts sheet compilation flags (\fB\-\-sheet\fR, \fB\-\-data\fR, \fB\-\-list\-tags\fR, \fB\-\-sheet\-type\fR).
.TP
.B godot
Natively generates Godot 4 \fBSpriteFrames\fR resources (\fB.tres\fR) with automatic sub-textures, animation sequences, unique stable UIDs, and exact pivot offset margins.
.TP
.B native
Default mode when invoked as \fBspritestudio-cli\fR, accepting both universal options and structured subcommands (\fBpack\fR, \fBslice\fR, \fBfilter\fR, \fBssp\fR).

.SH NATIVE SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B pack
Pack a list of image files or directories into an optimized 2D texture atlas using MaxRects or Tight Polygon heuristics.
.TP
.B slice
Segment and extract individual sprite frames from a static composite sheet using alpha flood-fill and connected-components analysis.
.TP
.B filter
Apply headless image processing filters (background removal, despill, outline, color swap, pixel rescale, retro palette quantization) to an atlas or sprite list.
.TP
.B ssp
Inspect, unpack, or export native SpriteStudio Project archives (\fB.ssp\fR).

.SH OPTIONS
.SS General Options
.TP
.B \-h\fR, \fB\-\-help
Display command-line help and usage summary.
.TP
.B \-v\fR, \fB\-\-version
Print version number, Git revision, and build configuration.
.TP
.B \-\-flavor \fIFLAVOR\fR
Force parser flavor: \fBtexturepacker\fR, \fBaseprite\fR, \fBgodot\fR, or \fBnative\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Format tool output as structured, machine-readable JSON on stdout.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet\fR, \fB\-q
Suppress non-essential log messages and progress indicators.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Enable detailed diagnostic and benchmark logging.
.TP
.B \-\-watch
Daemon mode: watch input files or directories and automatically regenerate exports upon filesystem modification.

.SS Packing & Sheet Layout Options
.TP
.B \-\-sheet \fIFILE\fR
Path to the output atlas image file (e.g., \fIatlas.png\fR, \fIatlas.webp\fR, \fIatlas.ktx2\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-data \fIFILE\fR
Path to the output metadata file (e.g., \fIatlas.json\fR, \fIatlas.tres\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-format \fIFORMAT\fR
Output data format. Supported: \fBjson\-array\fR, \fBjson\-hash\fR, \fBgodot\fR, \fBunity\fR, \fBunreal\fR, \fBxml\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-algorithm \fIALGO\fR
Packing algorithm: \fBmaxrects\fR (default) or \fBpolygon\fR (tight mesh).
.TP
.B \-\-heuristic \fIHEURISTIC\fR
MaxRects free rect heuristic: \fBBSSF\fR (Best Short Side Fit), \fBBLSF\fR (Best Long Side Fit), \fBBAF\fR (Best Area Fit).
.TP
.B \-\-pot
Force atlas dimensions to Power of Two powers (e.g., 512, 1024, 2048, 4096).
.TP
.B \-\-square
Force atlas width and height to be equal.
.TP
.B \-\-extrude \fIPIXELS\fR
Extrude sprite borders by \fIPIXELS\fR (typically 1) to eliminate bilinear filtering and mipmap bleeding.
.TP
.B \-\-padding \fIPIXELS\fR
Set border padding around each sprite in the atlas (default: 2).
.TP
.B \-\-trim\-mode \fIMODE\fR
Trimming mode: \fBCrop\fR (strip transparent pixels and store crop offsets) or \fBNone\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-deduplicate
Enable automatic frame deduplication (auto-aliasing). Identical frames share atlas space while preserving animation timelines.

.SS Tight Mesh & Polygon Packing Options
.TP
.B \-\-mesh\-mode \fIMODE\fR
Mesh mode: \fBtight\fR (concave/convex boundary) or \fBrect\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-max\-vertices \fIN\fR
Maximum vertex budget per sprite (range: 3 to 48, default: 16).
.TP
.B \-\-normal\-padding \fIFLOAT\fR
Outward normal dilation in pixels to prevent sharp art clipping (default: 1.5).
.TP
.B \-\-threads \fIN\fR
Number of concurrent worker threads for tight packing (default: logical CPU count).

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success. All requested assets were parsed, processed, and exported cleanly.
.TP
.B 1
General execution or configuration error.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line arguments or unknown option.
.TP
.B 3
Input file not found, unreadable, or corrupted.
.TP
.B 4
Packing failed: sprites could not fit into specified maximum dimensions.
.TP
.B 5
Output write error: disk full, permissions denied, or path invalid.

.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.B Example 1: Drop-in replacement for TexturePacker
.RS
.nf
spritestudio-cli --sheet characters.png --data characters.json \
  --format json-array --trim-mode Crop --extrude 1 raw_sprites/*.png
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B Example 2: Direct Godot 4 SpriteFrames generation
.RS
.nf
spritestudio-cli --sheet res://sprites/hero.png \
  --godot-tres res://sprites/hero_frames.tres \
  --trim --extrude 1 assets/hero_walk_*.png
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B Example 3: Continuous integration pipeline with JSON output
.RS
.nf
spritestudio-cli pack --sheet dist/atlas.png --data dist/atlas.json \
  --algorithm maxrects --pot --deduplicate --json assets/
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B Example 4: Watch daemon for live game reloading
.RS
.nf
spritestudio-cli --watch --sheet game/assets/atlas.png \
  --data game/assets/atlas.json src/sprites/
.fi
.RE

.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
.B QT_QPA_PLATFORM
Overridden internally to \fBoffscreen\fR by spritestudio-cli to ensure headless execution without a GUI display server.

